        <mxCell id="note_state" value="&lt;b&gt;Reading the hop state&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;TLS verified: the client checks the chain against a CA and checks the hostname. TLS unverified: the hop is encrypted, but the client does not check who answers (sslmode=require, or a driver default of prefer). Every database hop was read from pg_stat_ssl on Kind (2026-10-01): PgDog, Keycloak, PgBouncer and replication are TLS 1.3; Temporal and the OpenBao DB engine are plaintext. PLAINTEXT: nothing is encrypted on the hop. Operator-managed TLS (CNPG replication and the PgBouncer client cert, the OpenBao Raft cluster port, Envoy Gateway xDS, chart webhook Issuers) uses each operator's own CA, not homelab-ca. platform-db's backups take the same plaintext S3 path as product-db's. kubelet and kube-apiserver scrapes use TLS with insecureSkipVerify." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1525" width="1745" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_planned" value="&lt;b&gt;Planned, not installed (RFC-0020, provisional)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;S0 edge issuer decouple · S1 OpenBao listener TLS · S2 CNPG server cert from homelab-ca · S3 pooler TLS · S4 apps on sslmode=verify-full through a pooler · S5 per-hop client certs · S6 gRPC + Temporal mTLS. Added 2026-10-01: S7 intermediate CA · S8 Keycloak HTTPS · S9 platform-db clients · S10 Envoy BackendTLSPolicy · S11 RustFS TLS · S12 Valkey auth + TLS · S13 OCI registry TLS + cosign · S14 KMS over HTTPS (production)." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1607" width="1745" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
